  59:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** File    : SEGGER_RTT.c
  60:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** Purpose : Implementation of SEGGER real-time transfer (RTT) which
  61:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           allows real-time communication on targets which support
  62:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           debugger memory accesses while the CPU is running.
  63:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** Revision: $Rev: 12706 $
  64:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  65:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** Additional information:
  66:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           Type "int" is assumed to be 32-bits in size
  67:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           H->T    Host to target communication
  68:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           T->H    Target to host communication
  69:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  70:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           RTT channel 0 is always present and reserved for Terminal usage.
  71:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           Name is fixed to "Terminal"
  72:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  73:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           Effective buffer size: SizeOfBuffer - 1
  74:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  75:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff == RdOff:       Buffer is empty
  76:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff == (RdOff - 1): Buffer is full
  77:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff >  RdOff:       Free space includes wrap-around
  78:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           WrOff <  RdOff:       Used space includes wrap-around
  79:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****           (WrOff == (SizeOfBuffer - 1)) && (RdOff == 0):  
  80:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c ****                                 Buffer full and wrap-around after next byte
  81:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  82:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
  83:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  84:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
