 635:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 636:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 637:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 638:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block.
 639:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock does not lock the application 
 640:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    and overwrites data if the data does not fit into the buffer.
 641:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 642:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 643:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 644:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 645:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 646:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 647:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 648:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, data is overwritten.
 649:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
 650:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
 651:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
 652:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (3) Do not use SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock if a J-Link 
 653:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        connection reads RTT data.
 654:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
