 727:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** /*********************************************************************
 728:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 729:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_WriteSkipNoLock
 730:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 731:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 732:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 733:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block which is then read by the host.
 734:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteSkipNoLock does not lock the application and
 735:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    skips all data, if the data does not fit into the buffer.
 736:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 737:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 738:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 739:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 740:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 741:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 742:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 743:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
 744:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 745:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 746:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, all data is dropped.
 747:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
 748:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
 749:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
 750:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
