 872:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** /*********************************************************************
 873:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 874:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_WriteNoLock
 875:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 876:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 877:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 878:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block which is then read by the host.
 879:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteNoLock does not lock the application.
 880:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 881:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 882:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 883:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 884:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 885:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 886:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
 887:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
 888:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 889:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 890:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) Data is stored according to buffer flags.
 891:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
 892:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
 893:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
 894:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
