1013:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1014:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
1015:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a single character/byte in SEGGER RTT buffer.
1016:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_PutCharSkipNoLock does not lock the application and
1017:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    skips the byte, if it does not fit into the buffer.
1018:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1019:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
1020:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
1021:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    c            Byte to be stored.
1022:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1023:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Return value
1024:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Number of bytes which have been stored in the "Up"-buffer.
1025:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
1026:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
1027:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, the character is dropped.
1028:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
1029:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
1030:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
1031:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
1032:Core/SystemView/SEGGER_RTT.c **** 
